As explained in the new video for beginners about previous day strategy I have one question for example if we are looking for short trade, then if as explained in video that the second candle has to break the low if previous candle. My question is that  when the candle breaks the low of previous candle it mostly far away from the low that low so how will we have to enter into trade. Do we place limit order in the low of first red candle or we have to buy from current market. Even if we buy from current market then stoploss will be larger as it will cover two candle. In simple terms can you please explain some execution examples in video or short
